From 2a746b7515da6ee44f6adfb3f498d4496301ceba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:11:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: define the structured result of a functional test job

New test_framework/results.py: JobResult holds what the runner needs to
report one test job:
- status: passed, failed, skipped, timeout, crashed;
- exit code, start time and duration, phase timings;
- skip reason, failure (exception type, message, traceback);
- tmpdir and log paths;
- the last 200 lines of stdout and stderr.

Its JSON form is versioned ("schema": 1) and documented in
test/functional/README-runner-output.md.

Nothing produces or consumes it yet. The upcoming worker processes will
send it to the runner, and the console, JSON lines and JUnit reporters
will render it.

Unit tests cover the JSON round trip, status validation and output
tails. No behaviour change.
